```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: red
REAL_USE_CASE: No production operator needs a joint-dominance bounded-W scheduler. SGLang RadixAttention and vLLM APC already ship unbounded-greedy cache-aware admission (the prefill floor); bounded-W offers only a tunable fairness/prefill trade-off, not a strictly better frontier. A narrow future use case could be multi-tenant SLO enforcement where a p99 cap maps to an SLO, but that requires the pivoted metric (SLO-attainment-at-fixed-prefill) not evaluated in EXP-0007.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only. EXP-0007 (L0 CPU simulation) finds 0/36 cells with Bonferroni-significant joint dominance over both greedy and VTC. Greedy is the recomputed-prefill floor in 32/36 cells; bounded-W beats greedy on p99 in 13/36 cells but every win incurs a mandatory prefill cost (delta +1,109 to +38,229 tokens, mean +16,093). Bounded-W strictly dominates VTC in 36/36 cells, but greedy itself mean-dominates VTC on both axes in 31/36 cells under Zipf skew, showing VTC is the weak, non-deployed baseline. No evidence the partial VTC win survives on real hardware with paged KV, chunked prefill, or per-tenant SLO classes.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Production already defaults to SGLang-style greedy cache-aware admission (SGLang RadixAttention NeurIPS24, vLLM APC) — packet notes this is the right baseline; Adding a p99 skip-budget adds scheduler state/complexity without joint dominance; L0 is CPU-only simulation, authors state a GPU pass is required to measure real p99 TTFT and real prefill FLOPs on H100/MI350X; VTC is not a production baseline, so beating it is not compelling; Operators must tune W per workload, and the knob merely moves along the existing Pareto frontier rather than pushing it inward; No validation against real paged kernels, chunked prefill, or multi-SLO regimes.]
RATIONALE: EXP-0007 RESULTS.md reports joint-dominance win cells = 0/36 under Bonferroni FWER (m=864, alpha=5.79e-05). "Greedy is the recomputed-prefill FLOOR in 32/36 cells (by construction it maximizes reuse)" and "Bounded-W beats greedy on p99 (fairness) in 13/36 cells under FWER — but EVERY such p99 win comes with a strictly POSITIVE prefill cost (delta vs greedy: min +1109, max +38229, mean +16093 tokens)." "bounded-W STRICTLY DOMINATES VTC in 36/36 cells" but "Greedy itself mean-dominates VTC on both axes in 31/36 cells — under heavy skew, serving the hot (reuse-rich) families first is also roughly fair because they arrive most. VTC is the easy baseline to beat; greedy is the hard one." Authors note "This L0 is a queueing+cache SIMULATION, not the real systems" and "What a GPU pass should measure (L1+): Replace the abstraction with the REAL schedulers: SGLang RadixAttention greedy admission vs the real VTC implementation on vLLM/APC, on a real H100/MI350X, measuring real p99 TTFT (not simulated wait) and real recomputed prefill FLOPs/tokens" and "Add multi-SLO / priority classes (greedy has no notion of per-tenant SLO; bounded-W's p99 cap maps naturally to an SLO) — that is the regime where bounded-W could earn a real production case, but it changes the metric." Prior-art sweep owed for SGLang RadixAttention (NeurIPS24), VTC (OSDI24), Preble (packet "Prior-art caveat (sweep owed — no egress in this L0)"). Prompt version v001.
```
